  "id": "reconstructive-surgery",
  "term": "reconstructive surgery",
  "definition": "Reconstructive surgery is surgery used to repair or rebuild the body after burns or other injuries. In counselling contexts, it may be discussed because these often unexpected, life-changing injuries can be linked with increased emotional distress and other psychiatric difficulties.",
